If the claim that {{ atom_lc }} were so, then a specific, checkable consequence would follow: the public record of the period would read accordingly, and the established account — that {{ world_fact_lc }} — would have to give way. {{ frame_body }} But the established account does not give way; {{ world_fact }} Running that backwards: since the consequence that would have to hold does not hold, the antecedent cannot hold either. Hence {{ atom_lc_neg }}. The conditional is laid out here precisely so the failure of its consequent can be carried back onto its antecedent.

